$ enola constraints frobnicate
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola constraints <lint|mine|init|explain|ledger> [repo_path|config_path]

lint validates the declared constraint vocabulary — inline in enola-intent.yaml
and per-domain files under enola/constraints/ — and resolves each component
against the current snapshot, if one exists (else validation only).

mine searches the current snapshot's fact store for near-invariants and
reports them as candidate constraint declarations — proposals for operator
review, never self-adopting law. Run `enola constraints mine --help`.
init writes a first declaration binding every shipped recipe whose roles
resolve to directories the repository has. Run `enola constraints init --help`.
explain names the components a file's facts belong to, the selector that
admitted each, and the edges the file makes. Run `enola constraints explain --help`.
ledger reports how much of the declared law is being EXCUSED rather than
obeyed — every rule's breaches beside the suppressions and exemptions that
signed them away, with each excuse's owner and age. Run `enola constraints ledger --help`.

Exit codes (lint):
  0  every declaration is valid
  1  validation problems were reported
  2  the command could not run

Exit codes (mine, init, explain, ledger):
  0  a report was produced
  2  the command could not run — no snapshot to read, or a declaration
     init would have had to overwrite
